    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔥 Error Handler (global)\n\nFires when a subscribed workflow **hard-fails** (API rejection, credential error).\n\n**Subscribe a workflow**: its Settings → Error Workflow → this one.\nActive is not enough — nothing calls this without that pointer.\n\n**Does NOT catch expression errors.** n8n resolves a failed expression inside a\ntext field to an empty string and records the execution as `success`. Templates\nmust guard their own fields.\n\n**parse_mode: HTML** (Additional Fields). `error.message` is escaped inline —\n`&` first, then `<` and `>`, or the ampersand of `&lt;` gets re-escaped. Without\nit a `<` in an error message 400s Telegram and the crash alert itself vanishes.\n\n**Test**: set a subscriber's Telegram Chat ID to `1` → Publish → trigger it →\nTelegram returns 400 → this fires. Revert the Chat ID after.\n\nSubscribers: Backup Notification",
